/* book Worked example: Q: A buried channel guide has core thickness t = 0.5 µm, width w = 2 µm, n₁ = 1.50 and n₂ = 1.45 all round, used at λ = 1.55 µm. Find the NA of the index step and V for the thickness direction, and decide whether the thickness direction is single-mode.
   1. n₁² − n₂² = 2.2500 − 2.1025 = 0.1475, so NA = √0.1475 = 0.3841.
   2. 2πt/λ = 2π × 0.5/1.55 = 3.1416/1.55 = 2.027.
   3. V = 2.027 × 0.3841 = 0.778.
   4. The stack is symmetric (n₂ above and below), so the limit is π = 3.142. V = 0.778 < π: one mode across the thickness.
   Answer: NA = 0.384 and V = 0.778, well below π, so the thickness direction is single-mode. */
