/* book exam traps: The period a is one full pair of layers, not one layer. | n̄ in λB = 2n̄a is weighted by thickness. The plain mean of nH and nL is correct only when both layers have equal thickness. | The gap is a band of wavelengths, not one wavelength; λB is its centre. | Do not confuse the photonic band gap (a range of light wavelengths that cannot propagate) with a semiconductor's electronic band gap (an energy range with no electron states). | A band-gap fiber can guide in a hollow, lower-index core; an index-guiding PCF still needs the core index above the cladding's average. */
